  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Fan Tan (Sevens). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Fan Tan, also widely known as 'Sevens', 'Domino', or 'Parliament', is a classic layout-based card game where the objective is to be the first to get rid of all your cards. Players build upon a central layout of cards, starting with the Sevens and expanding outward to the Ace and Two in each suit. It is a game of both luck and light strategy, as players can choose to hold back key 'blocking' cards to prevent opponents from playing.",
    objective: 'Collect the highest value of awakened queens or the required number of queens.',
    gameplay: 'Players use number cards and action cards to awaken sleeping queen cards, defend their own queens, or affect opponents queens. Arithmetic card combinations and simple memory support the children’s game flow.',
    keyRules: [
      'Queen cards begin face down asleep.',
      'Kings awaken queens; other action cards steal, protect, or put queens back to sleep.',
      'The game ends by queen count, point total, or exhausted deck depending on player count.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
